Provenance of qrcodegen.js (kept here so the JavaScript stays byte-pinned)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream source:  https://www.nayuki.io/res/qr-code-generator-library/qrcodegen.js
Upstream size:    45,350 bytes
Upstream SHA-256: 2511bc17f40a3c41d4a0578995db956b38997334d3d20113a5d4dc5c49c69480

Adaptations, and only these:
1. Decoded as UTF-8 without a byte order mark.
2. Line endings normalised to CRLF.
3. Spaces and tabs removed at the end of lines 52, 640, 644, 790 and 816
   (parameter lists).
4. The existing final newline kept.
5. A blank line and "export { qrcodegen };" appended (CRLF-terminated).

Adapted file: 46,207 bytes with CRLF line endings, SHA-256
c5b15113a4ec416ba65d1a75acd664d74d8f187a081c46bb622590bef2f971c2 (informative).
With CRLF normalised to LF: 45,368 bytes, SHA-256
68453133c5cffbaebe89cdfba48f1bb0918535335bae75adfbdbfde2a8b318f5. This LF digest
is the portable one that tests/qr.test.js asserts.
